# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OMID Studio — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development (or set the variables
# in your hosting platform's dashboard) and fill in real values. Never commit
# a real .env / .env.local file. This example file is safe to commit — it
# contains only variable names and placeholder values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Path (absolute or relative to the server's working directory) where the
# project-inquiry JSON store lives. Defaults to `<project>/.data/inquiries.json`
# when unset. On a single always-running server this file persists across
# restarts; for deployments without a persistent filesystem (e.g. serverless
# or multiple instances), point this at a shared/database-backed store instead.
# OMID_STUDIO_DATA_FILE=/var/lib/omid-studio/inquiries.json

# Path where the privacy-limited analytics event stream is appended (JSONL).
# Defaults to `<project>/.data/analytics.ndjson` when unset. The file only ever
# holds validated, non-personal event records and is rotated once it grows
# large. Choose a persistent location on single-server deployments too.
# OMID_STUDIO_ANALYTICS_FILE=/var/lib/omid-studio/analytics.ndjson

# Set to 1 ONLY in production where TLS terminates (e.g. your reverse proxy
# terminates HTTPS). Enables Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS) and
# `upgrade-insecure-requests` in the Content-Security-Policy. Leave unset in
# local development / plain-http preview so nothing gets rewritten to https.
#
# NOTE: next.config.ts values are captured at BUILD time, so this flag must be
# set both when running `npm run build` and when running `npm run start` in
# production (e.g. `OMID_STUDIO_HTTPS_ENABLED=1 npm run build` then the same
# for start).
# OMID_STUDIO_HTTPS_ENABLED=1

# Example (server-only, unused today) — when inquiry emails are wired to a
# provider, the key lives here and never on the client:
# OMID_STUDIO_EMAIL_API_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Admin panel (Phase 11)
#
# Credentials for the /admin login. The panel is session-secured on its own
# (signed httpOnly cookie, rate-limited login), but keep both values strong
# and never commit them. Login fails closed when either is unset.
# OMID_STUDIO_ADMIN_USER=admin
# OMID_STUDIO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=use-a-strong-unique-password
#
# High-entropy secret used to sign admin session cookies. Recommended in
# production; when unset, a key is derived from the admin password. Changing
# this value signs out everyone currently logged in.
# OMID_STUDIO_AUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string
